# ::tok Recently, the United States' "chip war" against China has greatly escalated - first, the Netherlands and Japan agreed to start the control of the export of semiconductor manufacturing equipment to China under pressure from the United States; Later, foreign media reported that the US government is considering cutting off all contact between US suppliers and Huawei, and prohibiting US suppliers from providing any products to Huawei; The Biden administration is also preparing to issue an executive order restricting U.S. investment in sensitive Chinese tech sectors... Soon after the beginning of 2023, the United States has continued to make vicious moves to curb the development of China's semiconductor-related industries.
